Create a web page that contains a Student Feedback Form. Implement the following features-

1. Create a Form-
The form should contain the following fields:
Student Name (Text Box)
Email (Email Box)
Course (Dropdown)
Feedback (Textarea)

Also add the following buttons:
Submit Feedback
Delete Stored Data

2. Form Validation -
NO field should be left empty. If any field is left emptied, display error message.
Email should be in a valid format.

3. Display Error Messages
Display an appropriate error message below the respective field if the validation fails.
Error messages should disappear automatically when the user enters valid input.

4. Store Data in Local Storage
After successful validation:
Store the following details in Local Storage:
Student Name
Email
Course
Feedback
Display the stored information below the form.

5. Store Data in Session Storage
Store only the Student Name in Session Storage.
Display the message:
Current Session User: Student Name
The session data should be removed automatically after the browser tab is closed.(because it is session storage)

6. Delete Stored Data Button-
Remove all feedback details from Local Storage and Session Storage.
Display the message:
No feedback stored. 
